    "narrative": "The strongest play on the board today is **Lawrence Butler**, who commands an elite score of 74.57. While he is slotted seventh, the combination of a favorable matchup against Keller and a significant 10% boost from park factors and 13% from the platoon advantage makes him the centerpiece of our lineup. Following closely, **Bryson Stott** (70.11) and **Luis Arraez** (67.61) are priority starts. **Bryson Stott** benefits heavily from a 13% platoon boost against Phillips, while **Luis Arraez** leverages a premium leadoff spot and a 9% SP skill advantage to provide a stable, high-floor contribution for our AVG category.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the margins, where **Yainer Diaz** (56.22) narrowly squeezed into the starting rotation. While his raw base projection was moderate, he edged out **Masyn Winn** (50.66) because we must prioritize efficiency given our limited game caps. **Masyn Winn** remains a high-upside asset due to his elite SB potential, but his output is suppressed today by King\u2019s ability to control the basepaths, which negates some of his primary value. Conversely, **Taylor Ward** represents our highest risk today; he sits at a marginal 40.87, dragged down by a tough matchup against Gilbert and an unfavorable platoon split, making him the most likely candidate to be pulled if we need to preserve caps later in the week.\n\nWe are operating with a severely depleted roster due to the ongoing absences of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho**. This thin bench leaves us with limited room for maneuver, requiring us to ride players like **Jonathan Aranda** (46.95) despite his sub-50 score, as he is currently our best option to fill the 1B slot. We are keeping a close watch on **Geraldo Perdomo**, whose score of 50.71 is buoyed by his #2 spot in the order, though he faces a dangerous arm in Detmers. With **Tyler Freeman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Ryan Waldschmidt** currently unavailable or unplayable, the active roster must provide maximum efficiency to keep pace in the SB and AVG categories.",
